  "analysis": {
    "key_findings": [
      "INT8 dynamic PTQ does NOT insert QuantizeLinear/DequantizeLinear nodes into the ONNX graph. Instead, ORT applies quantization at runtime via ConvInteger + DynamicQuantizeLinear + Mul (dequant scale).",
      "Node expansion FP32\u2192INT8: MobileNetV2 2.86x (170\u2192487), ShuffleNetV2 1.37x (902\u21921240), EfficientNet-B0 3.05x (239\u2192730).",
      "DynamicQuantizeLinear nodes: MobileNetV2 53, ShuffleNetV2 54, EfficientNet-B0 82. MobileNetV2 has 53 depthwise separable convolutions that each require independent quantization.",
      "ORT profiling confirms quantization overhead (10 runs, batch=1, 1 thread): MobileNetV2 29.2%, ShuffleNetV2 20.7%, EfficientNet-B0 24.9% of total inference time spent on quant/dequant kernels.",
      "Conv_quant_kernel is the dominant bottleneck: MobileNetV2 55.1%, ShuffleNetV2 49.5%, EfficientNet-B0 54.5% of total time (per-operator us from ort_profiles; corrected 2026-09-26, previous 20.2/14.9/19.0 used a wrong denominator).",
      "DequantizeLinear is fused into Conv_quant kernel (not separate events in ORT profiling). The 29.2% quant overhead for MobileNetV2 correlates with its 30.1x INT8 slowdown vs 6.4x for ShuffleNetV2."
    ],
